  "assumptions": [
    "Every platform, event duration, capacity unit, repair duration and alternate-layer value in this fixture is synthetic; none is an empirical HAPS MTBF, MTTR, maintenance or service-capacity measurement.",
    "The 72-hour scenario is an event-trace oracle, not a statistical reliability model or 30-day service trial.",
    "Two service zones each require one unit of capacity and have equal demand weight; the service is available when demand-weighted delivery is at least 90%.",
    "A single active HAPS supplies one capacity unit to one named zone. A platform cannot supply two zones simultaneously.",
    "The planned-maintenance event affects haps-01 for six hours; the corrective-repair event affects haps-02 for ten hours.",
    "The common-cause weather event from hour 40 to hour 46 grounds all HAPS in the declared footprint; the event is correlated across the fleet, not independent platform failures.",
    "The two-spare rotation policy prepositions haps-03 for the planned maintenance interval and haps-04 for corrective repair; the fixture assumes handover is immediate at the interval boundary and does not model launch/transition lag.",
    "In the independent-fallback policy, a satellite layer supplies 0.95 capacity units to each zone during the common-cause weather interval; independence is an explicit synthetic scenario assumption, not measured availability or guaranteed atmospheric/space-network resilience.",
    "No alternate capacity is available in the no-spare and rotating-reserve-only policies during the common-cause event.",
    "Availability is elapsed time during which the total demand-weighted delivered fraction meets the threshold; time-weighted demand satisfaction is a separate integral metric.",
    "The 99.5% initial and 99.9% stretch targets refer to a separate 30-day service window and are Luminous research targets, not published industry commitments or achieved values.",
    "Maintenance/repair platform-hours are summed across assets; common-cause grounded platform-hours count each affected fleet platform for the full event duration.",
    "The fixture excludes stochastic failure/repair distributions, maintenance queueing, launch/recovery capacity, reserve readiness failure, crew/spares constraints, flight energy, thermal limits, wind, radio link quality, throughput, regulatory authority and physical operations."
  ]
}
